course: dictionary
lesson: 12835
title: Encase: covered all round
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: When something is encased, it is covered all round, like a sweet in its wrapper or a toy in a box. The word comes from case, which means a box or cover. Look at the clues around it: «The fly was encased in amber for millions of years.» Amber is hard and clear, and the fly is trapped inside it, so encase must mean covered all round.
explain: Encase is a verb, so its form changes: encase, encases, encased, encasing. «The lake is encased in ice this morning» tells you about now. «His broken arm was encased in plaster» tells you about something that already happened.
explain: To check your meaning, swap in a simple word. «The wires are encased in plastic» can become «the wires are covered in plastic», and the sentence still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
fact: Encase means to cover or surround something completely, as if in a case or box.
fact: Encase can also mean to put something inside a hard protective cover.
fact: «Encased» is the past form: «The fossil was encased in rock.»
fact: Fossils, insects and other things can be encased in rock, ice or amber.
fact: Wires are often encased in plastic to keep them safe.
exercise: «The insect was encased in amber for millions of years.» What does encased mean here? | *Covered all round by a hard material | Swept away by a river | Set free from a box | Painted bright yellow
exercise: «His broken arm was encased in plaster.» Which word is closest in meaning to encased? | Dropped | Lifted | *Covered | Opened
exercise: Find the word in this sentence that means covered completely: «The wires are encased in plastic to keep them safe.» | plastic | *encased | wires | safe
test: «The car was encased in ice after the storm.» What does encased mean? | Cleaned | Pushed over | *Completely covered | Lit up
test: Which form fits this sentence? «Every morning, the baker ___ the cakes in clear wrappers.» | encase | *encases | encasing | encased
exam: «The fossil was encased in rock for thousands of years, so scientists had to chip it free.» What does encased mean? | *Covered all round, as if in a box | Carried away by water | Drawn in pencil | Broken into small pieces
